Strongest objection: post-`x` verification detects failure but cannot prevent or undo killing the wrong shell. The operation remains an unavoidable TOCTOU race because `x` acts on current UI focus, not a stable target identity.

Initial marker position, row adjacency, and a second capture only reduce probability; none closes the race. Flip the default only after `x` can be bound atomically to the verified agent ID, or shell rows cannot receive destructive input through this flow.
